       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose ordered:** 4,250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg per day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin in adults is 2,550 mg per day (2,000 mg per day for extended-release). Single doses are typically 500\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This is about 5 times the maximum. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nIt may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day, the max)\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard strength\n- **500 mg** two or three times daily, or **1,000 mg** twice daily\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want, ideally with your resident or attending. Once you do, I'll enter it right away. If the high dose is intentional, I'd want that verified with the supervising physician and pharmacy first."
