      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 12,750 mg per day is about five times the maximum daily dose, and there's no clinical scenario where that is appropriate. It could cause severe lactic acidosis and serious harm to the patient. A student's confirmation also isn't the right check for an order like this.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day, the maximum), or a lower starting dose such as 500 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Add a note for review.** If you think a different dose was intended, I can add a note asking your resident or attending to verify it.\n\nIf your attending really does want a dose outside the labeled range, they should enter or co-sign it themselves. Pharmacy would also need to review it. Tell me which standard dose you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
